          "candId": "chemistry-2021-HL-scheme-q4h",
          "src": "/exam-figures/chemistry/markbank/chemistry-2021-HL-scheme-q4h.png",
          "srcHash": "de6c0ff3ff8a7d051b3442889478b0a0",
          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2021 HL Q4(h), as the State Examinations Commission set it: FIND 3 / KBrO₃ (6): 80 over (39 + 80 + 16x) = 0.479 / 80 over (119 + 16x) × 100 = 47.9 (3), 80 = 57.001 + 7.664x ⇒ x = 3 (3); or 39 over 80 × 47.9 = 23.35% (23.4%) K and 100 − (47.9 + 23.4) = 28.7% (28.8%, 29%) O (3), 47.9 over 80 = 0.598, 23.4 over 39 = 0.6, 28.7 over 16 = 1.794, 0.598 : 0.6 : 1.794 = 1 : 1 : 3 ⇒ x = 3 (3); or 80 = 47.9 % ⇒ 167.01 = 100 = Mr (3), 167.01 − 80 − 39 = 48.01 = 16x ⇒ x = 3 (3); [*Work based on Ar values in Formula and Tables booklet acceptable.]",
