    section: "B", questionRef: "2021 HL Q9(c)(i)",
    stem: "In the Haber process the following chemical equilibrium is established using an iron catalyst. N₂ (g) + 3H₂ (g) ⇌ 2NH₃ (g) The graph shows how, starting with N₂ and H₂ in a 1:3 molar ratio, the percentage NH₃ by volume at equilibrium varies with temperature for three different pressures. When 9.0 moles nitrogen and 27.0 moles hydrogen were placed in a 10.0 litre container, there were 6.0 moles ammonia present when equilibrium was reached at temperature T.",
