          "alt": "A line graph. The y-axis is labelled \"% Ammonia at Equilibrium\" with ticks at 0, 20, 40, 60, 80 and 100; the x-axis is labelled \"Temperature (K)\" with ticks at 373, 473, 573, 673, 773 and 873. Faint grey gridlines cross the plot area. Three curves all fall from left to right: a fine dotted curve that starts at 100%, stays high to about 573 K and is still near 30% at 873 K, labelled \"100 MPa\"; a solid curve that starts near 98%, falls steeply through the middle of the range and reaches about 8% at 873 K, labelled \"20 MPa\"; and a heavy dashed curve that starts near 90%, drops very steeply and lies almost flat on the axis from about 673 K, labelled \"1 MPa\". Three grey square boxes with bold black capitals sit on the plot: box A on the far left just below the 80% line at the 373–473 K end; box B near the top of the plot at about 573 K, just under the dotted 100 MPa curve; and box C on the right at roughly 20% near 773 K, on the solid 20 MPa curve. Beneath the plot the line \"(a) Select the area of the graph (box A, B or C) corresponding to the conditions most\" runs to the crop's lower edge and its sentence continues off-crop.",
