    stem: "Succinic acid and its salts are food additives. The formula of a molecule of succinic acid is (CH₂)ₙ(COOH)₂ where n > 1. Succinic acid reacts with sodium hydroxide according to the following balanced equation: (CH₂)ₙ(COOH)₂ + 2NaOH → (CH₂)ₙ(COONa)₂ + 2H₂O When 1.77 g of succinic acid react completely with sodium hydroxide 2.43 g of (CH₂)ₙ(COONa)₂ (disodium succinate) are formed.",
