    questionText: "Tetraethyllead burns completely according to the equation: 2(C₂H₅)₄Pb (l) + 27O₂ (g) → 16CO₂ (g) + 20H₂O (l) + 2PbO (s) The heats of formation of tetraethyllead, carbon dioxide, water and lead(II) oxide are 52.7, –393.5, –285.8 and –219.0 kJ mol⁻¹ respectively. Calculate the heat of reaction for the combustion of one mole of tetraethyllead.",
