    stem: "Consider the equilibrium represented by the following balanced equation. 2BrCl (g) ⇌ Br₂ (g) + Cl₂ (g) yellow red‐brown green",
    questionText: "Calculate the percentage decomposition into bromine and chlorine of 0.200 moles of BrCl, placed initially in a 5 litre closed container, and allowed to reach equilibrium at 1200 °C according to the equation above. Take the value of Kc at this temperature as 0.220. Give your answer correct to the nearest whole number.",
