          "alt": "The marking scheme's own print of its answer to 2018 HL Q6(b)(iii), as the State Examinations Commission set it: –1239.1 kJ mol⁻¹ (12); boxed, ΔHcombustion = ΣΔHf(products) – ΣΔHf(reactants); = –571.6 kJ (3) + [(–393.5) + (–296.8)] kJ (3) – (–22.8 kJ) (3); or = –571.6 kJ (3) [–393.5 –296.8] kJ (3) + 22.8 kJ (3); or = –1261.9 kJ (6) + 22.8 kJ (3); and = –1239.1 kJ mol⁻¹ (3); \"[+1239.1 by this method is not a slip and is worth maximum (9).]\" and \"[+1239.1 with no work shown is worth (3).]\"; \"or\"; boxed, 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O ΔH = –571.6 kJ (3); C + O₂ → CO₂ ΔH = –393.5 kJ and S + O₂ → SO₂ ΔH = –296.8 kJ, bracketed together (3); CH₃SH → C + 2H₂ + S ΔH = 22.8 kJ (3); CH₃SH + 3O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O + SO₂ ΔH = –1239.1 kJ mol⁻¹ (3); \"Equations not essential, however:\"; \"Final Answer: CO₂ + 2H₂O + SO₂ → CH₃SH + 3O₂ ΔH = +1239.1 kJ is worth (9) marks with this equation\"; \"Final Answer: +1239.1 kJ is worth (3) marks if accompanied by no equation or by an equation other than that for combustion in reverse: (CO₂ + 2H₂O + SO₂ → CH₃SH + 3O₂).\"",
          "attribution": "SEC Leaving Certificate Chemistry 2018 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission",
          "solution": true,
